<title>GERMANY: Telekom details allotment to retail clients.</title>
<headline>Telekom details allotment to retail clients.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications group Deutsche Telekom AG gave the following details of share allocations which will be made to private investors (denominated in number of shares) -</p>
<p>    Buy order	 AIF registrees (*)     Other orders</p>
<p>    Under 100	 total order		total order up</p>
<p>							 to maximum of 50</p>
<p>    100		 100			  50</p>
<p>    101 - 149	 100			  50</p>
<p>    150 - 199	 110			  50</p>
<p>    200		 120			  60</p>
<p>    201 - 249	 120			  60</p>
<p>    250 - 299	 140			  70</p>
<p>    300		 160			  80</p>
<p>    301 - 349	 160			  80</p>
<p>    350 - 399	 180			  90</p>
<p>    400 - 449	 200			  100</p>
<p>    450 - 499	 220			  110</p>
<p>    500		 230			  110</p>
<p>    501 - 549	 230			  110</p>
<p>    550 - 599	 240			  120</p>
<p>    600 - 999	 250			  120</p>
<p>    1000		300			  150</p>
<p>    1001 - 1999     300			  150</p>
<p>    2000 - 4999     500			  250</p>
<p>    5000 - 9999     800			  400</p>
<p>    ab 10.000	 1000			 500</p>
<p>NOTE (*) - Would-be shareholders who registered at Telekom's share information centre (AIF) by November 6 were entitled to discounted shares and other benefits, such as the preferential allocation rate shown here.</p>
<p>--William Boston, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
